Nina: FYI opened PR to modernize streaming snippets + add a concise cross-language backoff example: https://github.com/redwood-inference/docs/pull/3991. Preview renders but I want a sanity-check on the wording that separates streaming vs pagination and clarifies retry semantics.

Alec: Quick pass looks good. A few notes: call out that streaming yields incremental deltas (token/chunk stream) while pagination returns full page snapshots via next_token. I added a one-liner: "streaming = incremental deltas; pagination = discrete pages (next_token)".

Alec: Python example we show uses a generator consumer pattern:```python
for chunk in client.chat.stream(req):
    if getattr(chunk, 'throttle_hint', False):
        # advisory: caller-level backoff recommended
        time.sleep(0.5)
        continue
    sys.stdout.write(chunk.text)
```
Add note: throttle_hint is advisory, not an infra guaranteed retry signal.

Priyanka: TS snippet uses an async iterator and demonstrates surfacing rate-limit responses instead of throwing:```ts
for await (const part of client.chat.stream(req)) {
  if (part.error?.code === 'RATE_LIMIT') {
    // surface to caller for custom backoff
    continue
  }
  appendToDom(part.text)
}
```
I added a tiny paragraph that recommends using a caller-level exponential backoff policy for RATE_LIMIT and 429s.

Nina: Can we include a short, language-agnostic pseudocode block for exponential backoff (1-2 lines) before each per-SDK sample?

Alec: Yup, suggested:```text
on RATE_LIMIT:
  wait = min(max_wait, base * 2**attempt)
  sleep(wait)
  retry
```
Callout: this is a caller-level policy; the platform may also perform automatic retries for transient infra errors.

Priyanka: Go sample currently uses a Receive loop; I refactored to a simple iterator-like pattern and added ctx cancellation guidance:```go
stream, err := client.Stream(ctx, req)
if err != nil { return err }
for {
  chunk, ok := stream.Recv()
  if !ok { break }
  if chunk.Err != nil {
    // surface error and let caller decide (log/backoff/return)
    continue
  }
  fmt.Print(chunk.Text)
}
```
Note: explicitly mention "respect ctx cancellation and avoid spinning unbounded goroutines per stream".

Nina: I also found an old anchor in the migration guide linking to `#old-streams`. I updated it to `#streaming-patterns` and left a 1-line redirect note in the markdown.

docs-bot: Preview deployed: https://docs-preview.redwood.ai/pr-3991  build passed :white_check_mark:

